% ============================================================================
% plant-need.query.adj — a worked recall over the plant-need library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what does sunlight do
% for a plant?": it states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?`
% against the `plant_need` rows and returns the role + the table's own
% source/locator/trust. An input the table does not carry abstains
% honestly — the engine never invents a role.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli plant-need.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "plant-need.adj"

? plant_need(sunlight, $Role)              % expect excites_chlorophyll_electrons
? plant_need($Need, combined_to_make_glucose)  % expect carbon_dioxide
? plant_need(soil, $Role)                  % expect abstain — no role is shipped for soil
